<%# locals: (missing:, colspan:) %>
<%# The ruled short page (doc/wissen_als_bahn_plan.md, section 13, D8): for
    every row the page has room for but the list did not fill, one empty row
    across the whole table. The line and the height are not drawn here: every
    cell of a list table carries them (layout.css, ".list table td" and
    ".list table tr td"), so the ruling continues the rows' own rhythm. This
    partial only supplies the rows, and it is the ONE place that does; a
    third hand-written loop is what CLAUDE.md's "same rule enforced by hand"
    is about.
    ⚠️ colspan is the whole reason this exists as a partial. The ticket table
    padded itself the same way until #768 and had lost the colspan on the way
    (a882a25a): the cell then spanned the first column only, and the divider
    under it drew a short dash per phantom row down the left edge, which read
    as a defect and cost the table its ruling. The caller hands over the count
    of its header cells; the request specs hold the two together.
    Decoration, so no reader and no keyboard meets it: aria-hidden, no
    tabindex, no controller, no identity attribute anything counts rows by. %>
<% [missing.to_i, 0].max.times do %>
  <tr class="ruled-line" data-ruled-line aria-hidden="true"><td colspan="<%= colspan %>">&nbsp;</td></tr>
<% end %>
